      "updated_at": "2026-04-06T06:11:29Z",
      "body": "<img width=\"2126\" height=\"627\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a6dad06c-a92a-4d88-9940-0f03ddb6687e\" />\n\nThanks for the report. Our experiments were conducted on **8×A800 GPUs**, and the results in the paper are based on that exact setup.\n\n\"Adapting to your workstation\" likely involves changes to the number of GPUs, batch size, or gradient accumulation steps, which directly affect training dynamics and are **not trivial modifications**. For reference, we attach our training curves above, which look quite different from yours. This is more consistent with a misconfigured training setup rather than a code bug.\n\nWe'd suggest double-checking that your effective batch size and distributed training configuration match the original settings provided in the training scripts in this repository.",
